---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Mailbox from "../components/Mailbox.astro";
import ArticleCard from "../components/ArticleCard.astro";

const latest = (await getCollection("blog"))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.getTime() - a.data.pubDate.getTime())
  .slice(0, 3);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="TempMail — A temporary inbox, when you need one"
  description="Create a real temporary email address, receive messages, and keep your everyday inbox separate. No account required."
>
  <div class="page-wrap home-page">
    <Mailbox />

    <section class="editorial-section explainer-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">A small tool, clearly explained</p><h2>Temporary email, without the fuss.</h2></div>
        <p>Use a separate inbox when a form asks for an email address but a lasting relationship is not what you want.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-grid">
        <article><span class="principle-number">01</span><h3>Get an address</h3><p>TempMail asks Guerrilla Mail to create an actual mailbox and returns the address it provides.</p></article>
        <article><span class="principle-number">02</span><h3>Wait for a message</h3><p>The inbox checks for new mail every 30 seconds while this page is open. Refresh whenever you like.</p></article>
        <article><span class="principle-number">03</span><h3>Use it briefly</h3><p>Addresses are temporary. The provider documents a 60-minute address lifetime and supports limited extensions.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="editorial-section privacy-section">
      <div class="privacy-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Know what you are using</p>
        <h2>A buffer, not a cloak.</h2>
        <p>A disposable address can keep low-stakes sign-ups out of your everyday inbox. It does not make you anonymous, encrypt messages, or protect an account you use it to create.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">Read how mailbox data is handled <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <img src="/images/online-privacy.svg" alt="" width="960" height="420" loading="lazy" />
    </section>

    <section class="editorial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Good fits</p><h2>When might a temporary inbox help?</h2></div>
      </div>
      <ul class="use-case-list">
        <li><strong>One-off downloads</strong><span>Keep a receipt or link separate from your main mailbox.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Trying a service</strong><span>Use an address you do not plan to keep for a low-risk trial.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Testing email flows</strong><span>Receive a verification message while checking a non-production workflow.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="caution-note">Do not use a temporary inbox for banking, health services, password recovery, or accounts you need to keep. Anyone who can access the same address may be able to receive future mail.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="editorial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Common questions</p><h2>Before you start</h2></div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/faq/">All questions <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details><summary>Is this a real email address?</summary><p>Yes. The address comes from Guerrilla Mail. This site sends requests to its documented API through a same-origin Cloudflare Function.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How long does it last?</summary><p>Guerrilla Mail documents a 60-minute lifetime for a non-subscriber address, with extensions subject to its limits. An inactive provider session may expire sooner.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I use it for a private account?</summary><p>No. Do not use shared temporary mail for sensitive accounts or password recovery. It is not a private or anonymous mailbox.</p></details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="editorial-section latest-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">From the notes</p><h2>Latest articles</h2></div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/blog/">Visit the blog <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="article-card-grid">{latest.map((post) => <ArticleCard post={post} />)}</div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
